## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: reimporting an OKF bundle silently replaces an existing wiki concept with damaged text when its source contains malformed UTF-8.

## User Impact

User impact: malformed concept sources produce an actionable warning while valid concepts continue importing and existing pages are retained. An unreadable root `index.md` stops the import before concept writes; repair its encoding and retry.

## Why This Change Was Made

Validate the bytes returned by the existing guarded file reader before decoding. Reuse `unreadable-entry` and the existing warning-based pruning protection. Treat an unreadable present root index separately from a missing index, so its bundle identity cannot silently fall back to a different value.

No new options, dependencies, config/protocol/schema changes, or migrations. This concerns bundle input decoding; #175707 separately preserves human Notes when writing imported pages.

