## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: piped malformed UTF-8 can silently shorten a manually pasted model token or API key and overwrite the usable saved credential.

## User Impact

User impact: both noninteractive paste commands fail before credential/config writes when the byte input is malformed; valid input keeps its existing normalization.

No config defaults, storage schema, protocol, permissions, migrations, or upgrade behavior change.

## Why This Change Was Made

Validate the complete bounded stdin buffer before text decoding. Offline paste commands and the running-Gateway API-key adapter share this manual-input reader, so malformed bytes cannot become altered credential text. The existing reader and stdin test fixtures move into their existing input owner/support module to keep the affected files within the repository growth guard.

