## What Problem This Solves

A targeted `openclaw system event --session-key … --mode now` was queued for the base session but omitted from the prompt when the heartbeat ran in an isolated session. The CLI producer sends this wake with source `manual`, while the prompt resolver only admitted `notifications-event`.

This change admits targeted `manual` wakes through the existing targeted-unscheduled-wake check, so the event reaches the isolated heartbeat and is consumed.

Fixes #175599

## Why This Change Was Made

The system-event CLI uses the same immediate targeted-wake contract already recognized by `isTargetedUnscheduledWake`. Applying that guard to both `manual` and `notifications-event` covers the actual producer and keeps other wake sources on their existing queue path. The regression includes a disabled cadence (`heartbeat.every: "0m"`).

## User Impact

An explicitly targeted background event now appears in the isolated heartbeat model input and is consumed. A routine event remains queued during an ordinary isolated wake.

